# 7. DESIGN SYSTEM

Define everything as tokens (CSS variables or the existing styling system) and document in docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md.
- Color: base ink starting at #090D16 with 3-4 lifted surface steps; one warm thermal accent for trace and active states; muted blue-gray for structure; paper off-white for receipt and Plain surfaces. Status encoding is never color-only. Verify contrast for every text/background pair. Avoid purple or cyan gradients, neon glow, glassmorphism, floating particles and generic dashboard cards unless justified for this concept.
- Type: at most two families (a variable grotesque and a mono with tabular numerals), self-hosted or from the existing font setup, font-display: swap, metric-matched fallbacks, roughly 100 KB total at most. Fluid scale with clamp(); body line length 60-75ch.
- Spacing and grid: 8px base unit; 12-column desktop, 8-column tablet, 4-column mobile; content max width about 1280px, wider canvases permitted.
- Surfaces and depth: hairline 1px rules, tick marks and dimension-style labels; depth through overlap only; a restrained shadow only on receipt surfaces.
- Motion: tokens for duration (120/200/320ms) and easing. Principle: things trace, print and settle. No parallax. Every animation has a purpose, a reduced-motion variant and an off-screen pause.
- Icons: a small custom inline SVG set with 1.5px stroke; no icon library sprawl.
- States: default, hover (pointer only), focus-visible (at least 2px ring with offset), active, disabled, loading (skeleton or static placeholder preventing layout shift), error (plain-language message with a recovery action), empty.
- Different content types get different representations (diagrams, receipt, list, graph) while feeling like one system.

# 8. RESPONSIVE REQUIREMENTS

Verify at 360, 390, 430, 768, 1024, 1440 and 1920px widths.
- 360-430: single column; top progress bar with stratum label; simplified or static diagrams; Atlas as filter chips plus list plus focused neighbor view; Lab controls beneath the canvas; no hover dependence; respect safe-area insets; use svh/dvh instead of 100vh.
- 768: two-column where it helps; Atlas as list plus canvas split.
- 1024+: side rail; full Atlas canvas with detail panel (if gated in).
- 1440 and 1920: constrained text measure, composed (not stretched) layouts; no empty-looking voids.
- Reduce effects on low-power devices: if more than 30 consecutive frames exceed 24ms, automatically drop to a simplified visual mode.
- No horizontal page scroll at any width; wide tables and diagrams scroll inside their own container.

# 9. ACCESSIBILITY (WCAG 2.2 AA target)

Semantic landmarks, a skip link, one h1, logical heading order; keyboard access to every function with visible focus; prefers-reduced-motion honored everywhere; prefers-contrast and forced-colors do not break the layout; any motion longer than 5 seconds has a pause control; no flashing; text alternatives for every informational graphic; aria-live used sparingly and throttled; do not rely on color, hover or drag alone; touch targets as in 6.2; meaningful alt text.

# 10. PERFORMANCE

Measure a baseline first. Targets (mobile, throttled): LCP at most 2.5s, INP at most 200ms, CLS at most 0.1. Initial-route JavaScript must not grow by more than about 60 KB gzipped over baseline; lazy-load Atlas and Lab. Compress and size images; modern formats; no unoptimized hero media. Preload only the critical font; no layout shift from fonts. Animations use transform and opacity; pause offscreen; clean up listeners and rAF loops on unmount. If Lighthouse is runnable, target mobile Performance 90+, Accessibility 95+, Best Practices 95+, SEO 90+ as a minimum, not as proof of quality.

